  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and takes about 55 minutes from start to finish. The meatballs are browned in a frying pan first to build colour, then transferred to the tomato sauce to finish cooking through and absorb the flavour of the sauce."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Do not overwork the mince when mixing. Stir only until the ingredients just come together: overworked meat makes dense, tough meatballs. Roll with lightly wet hands to stop the mixture sticking, and aim for walnut-sized balls so they cook evenly."
          }
        ]
      },
