            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "albondigas"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Albondigas"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " appear across the Spanish-speaking world in many forms, but the Spanish version with smoked paprika and tomato is perhaps the most well-known. They are served as tapas in small portions or as a main course with crusty bread to mop up the sauce. The dish improves overnight as the meatballs absorb more of the sauce. Make it the day before if you can."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
